I had a pretty good game going. Level 30 Lawful Priest with 500+ HP
(Thanks to all the Wraiths of the Priest Quest), about 20 spells 
memorized, a pet Archon, all sorts of neat toys including:
 Armor: Speed boots, Sheild of reflection, Crystal Plate mail,
        Rustproof Gauntlets of Power, ...
 Weapons: +5 Excalibur, +4 Sunsword, +0? Demonbane, 
          +0? Trollsbane,...
 Rings: Polymorph Control, Polymorph, Conflict, Regeneration, ...

So I get to the end of the quest.  My Archon and I killed the other
monsters, and then started on WhatsHisName.  He took off upstairs
leaving the Mitre behind.  So I took it, and went up after him
with my Archon.  We killed him and got the bell of opening.

At this point things went wrong (all good nethack stories end in
tragedy).

My Archon disappeared (I think he fell through a trap door), and
WhatsHisName reappeared.  He blew up all the armor listed above
(leaving me with a +2 Hawaiian Shirt, The Mitre, and maybe 
one other thing), then he summoned a bunch of nasties (a Dragon
and a few other things).

Life without speed boots and Gauntlets of power was quite slow.
I saw half my hit points disappear, so I decided to get out of 
that vicinity.  I read a spell of teleport, hoping I'd wind up
near the upstairs, so I could prevent WhatHisName from recovering
there.  I landed away from all the nasties, but not anywhere near 
the stairs.

I ran for the stairs, WhatsHisName appeared, and I bashed him a 
couple of times, and then noticed I was at 5 Hit points.  I
confess to being a hack and slasher at heart, so I decided to
hit him again.  As you've probably guessed, I didn't kill him
with that final hit - game over.


Please don't point out all the mistakes I made on that level -
there were many (it was getting quite late). Obvious ones:
 - I should have stayed closer to my Archon
 - When WhatHisName surrounded me with nasties, I should have used
   my charm monster spell.
 - When I was at 5 HP, I should have prayed (I was in great standing
   with my god).

Ah well.
